1. EXECUTIVE ARCHITECTURAL SPECIFICATION
================================================================================
CyberBreak is a military-grade defensive, anti-tracking, and anti-forensic security 
workstation suite architected specifically for Kicksecure Linux (and hardened Debian). 

It is engineered as a first-class native Linux desktop application:
- Seamlessly integrates into GNOME, XFCE, KDE, and Kicksecure Whisker/App grids.
- 1-click creation of trusted desktop launchers (`~/Desktop/cyberbreak.desktop`).
- Native Polkit authentication (`pkexec`) prompt on launch—never requires terminal hacks.
- Zero mock/fake data: all monitors query real Netlink sockets, sysfs, procfs, 
  iptables/nftables, AppArmor, D-Bus, and raw block devices.
- Non-blocking asynchronous threading architecture (QThread + Signals/Slots) ensuring 
  zero GUI lockups during network audits or intensive crypto-wipes.

